IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cp6-interpretation`

-- Tests of cp6-interpretation.l4 (section 91 and subsections 104(1) and (2)).

§ `Tests -- the definitions of Part III`

§§ `Section 91: the portions that make up the additional Canada Pension Plan`

-- The twelve provisions the definition names are each part of the additional plan; any other portion is not.
#ASSERT `s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` `the portion referred to in paragraph 46(1)(b)`
#ASSERT `s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` `the portion referred to in paragraph 46(1)(c)`
#ASSERT `s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` `the portion referred to in subparagraph 56(1)(b)(ii)`
#ASSERT `s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` `the portion referred to in subparagraph 56(1)(b)(iii)`
#ASSERT `s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` `the portion referred to in clause 58(1)(a)(ii)(B)`
#ASSERT `s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` `the portion referred to in clause 58(1)(a)(ii)(C)`
#ASSERT `s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` `the portion referred to in clause 58(1)(a.1)(ii)(B)`
#ASSERT `s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` `the portion referred to in clause 58(1)(a.1)(ii)(C)`
#ASSERT `s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` `the portion referred to in subparagraph 58(1)(b)(ii)`
#ASSERT `s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` `the portion referred to in subparagraph 58(1)(b)(iii)`
#ASSERT `s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` `the portion referred to in subsection 59.1(3)`
#ASSERT `s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` `the portion referred to in subsection 59.1(5)`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` `any other portion of a benefit`)

-- The base plan is what the additional plan leaves.
#ASSERT `s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the base Canada Pension Plan` `any other portion of a benefit`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the base Canada Pension Plan` `the portion referred to in paragraph 46(1)(b)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 91 — a portion of a benefit is part of the base Canada Pension Plan` `the portion referred to in subsection 59.1(5)`)

-- Contributions follow the portions they are in respect of.
#ASSERT `s 91 — a contribution is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 91 — a contribution is part of the additional Canada Pension Plan` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 91 — a contribution is part of the base Canada Pension Plan` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 91 — a contribution is part of the base Canada Pension Plan` TRUE)

§§ `Section 91: Minister`

#ASSERT `s 91 — the Minister of Part III` EQUALS `the Minister of Employment and Social Development`

§§ `Subsection 104(1): administration, federal institution, public officer`

-- "includes the development, operation, evaluation and enforcement of policies and programs"
#ASSERT `s 104(1) — an activity is administration` `the development of policies and programs` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 104(1) — an activity is administration` `the operation of policies and programs` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 104(1) — an activity is administration` `the evaluation of policies and programs` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 104(1) — an activity is administration` `the enforcement of policies and programs` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not covered: "includes" leaves the rest of the ordinary meaning open.
#ASSERT `s 104(1) — an activity is administration` `another activity` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Inputs: the body is a department; the body is referred to in Schedule I, I.1, II or III to the Financial Administration Act.
#ASSERT `s 104(1) — a body is a federal institution` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 104(1) — a body is a federal institution` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 104(1) — a body is a federal institution` FALSE FALSE)

-- Inputs: officer or employee of a federal institution; an individual a regulation prescribes; a member of a class a regulation prescribes.
#ASSERT `s 104(1) — a person is a public officer` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 104(1) — a person is a public officer` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 104(1) — a person is a public officer` FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 104(1) — a person is a public officer` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Subsection 104(2): the definitions apply in sections 104, 104.1 and 105 only`

#ASSERT `s 104(2) — a definition in subsection 104(1) governs the provision` `section 104`
#ASSERT `s 104(2) — a definition in subsection 104(1) governs the provision` `section 104.1`
#ASSERT `s 104(2) — a definition in subsection 104(1) governs the provision` `section 105`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 104(2) — a definition in subsection 104(1) governs the provision` `any other provision of the Act`)
